––– comment –––
Shared bulk_import into a sharded table that Buddy created with shards='4' rf='1' on one node: the
physical shards live in the system database, every shard gets one child and one chunk,
every row lands where an ordinary write routes its id. The daemon gets threads = 8 for any CPU
count of the runner.
––– input –––
sed -i '/^searchd *{/a threads = 8' /etc/manticoresearch/manticore.conf
––– output –––
––– block: ../../base/start-searchd-with-buddy –––
––– input –––
mysql -h0 -P9306 -e "CREATE TABLE bb (title TEXT, gid INT, price FLOAT, tags MULTI, j JSON) shards='4' rf='1'"; echo $?
––– output –––
0
––– input –––
cat > /tmp/bb.sh <<'EOF'
sql() { mysql -h0 -P9306 --skip-table --batch --raw --skip-column-names -e "$1"; }
post() { curl -sS -X POST "http://localhost:9308/bulk?bulk_import=bb&shared" -H 'Content-Type: application/x-ndjson' --data-binary @"$1" -w ' HTTP %{http_code}\n'; }
commit() { printf '\n' > /tmp/commit.ndjson; post /tmp/commit.ndjson; }
counts() { echo "$(sql "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM bb") = $(for t in 0 1 2 3; do sql "SELECT COUNT(*) FROM system.bb_s$t"; done | paste -sd+)"; }
EOF
––– output –––
––– input –––
source /tmp/bb.sh; for ((i=1; i<=4000; i++)); do printf '{"insert":{"table":"bb","id":%d,"doc":{"title":"doc %d","gid":%d,"price":%d.5,"tags":[%d,%d],"j":{"k":%d}}}}\n' $i $i $((i%7)) $i $i $((i+1)) $i; done > /tmp/bb.ndjson; post /tmp/bb.ndjson; echo "children=$(ps -eo args | grep -c '[i]ndexer_rt_bulk_chunk')"; counts
––– output –––
{"items":[],"current_line":4000,"skipped_lines":0,"errors":false,"error":"","error_code":"","shared_state":"staged"} HTTP 200
children=4
0 = 0+0+0+0
––– input –––
source /tmp/bb.sh; commit; counts; echo "disk chunks: $(for t in 0 1 2 3; do sql "SELECT * FROM system.bb_s$t.@status" | wc -l; done | paste -sd' ')"; sql "SELECT COUNT(*), SUM(id), SUM(gid) FROM bb; SELECT id, title, gid, price, tags, j FROM bb WHERE id IN (1, 4000) ORDER BY id ASC"; echo "children=$(ps -eo args | grep -c '[i]ndexer_rt_bulk_chunk')"
––– output –––
{"items":[],"current_line":1,"skipped_lines":0,"errors":false,"error":"","error_code":"","shared_state":"published"} HTTP 200
4000 = 987+997+965+1051
disk chunks: 1 1 1 1
4000	8002000	11997
1	doc 1	1	1.500000	1,2	{"k":1}
4000	doc 4000	3	4000.500000	4000,4001	{"k":4000}
children=0
––– comment –––
I1: REPLACE through the sharded table changes no count of any shard.
––– input –––
source /tmp/bb.sh; sql "REPLACE INTO bb (id, title, gid) VALUES (1,'r',0),(2,'r',0),(3,'r',0),(4,'r',0),(5,'r',0),(6,'r',0),(7,'r',0),(8,'r',0)"; counts
––– output –––
4000 = 987+997+965+1051
––– comment –––
PURGE BULK_IMPORT by the sharded table name cancels a load; a direct Shared request into a shard of
an open load is refused.
––– input –––
source /tmp/bb.sh; for ((i=5001; i<=5040; i++)); do printf '{"insert":{"table":"bb","id":%d,"doc":{"title":"p %d","gid":1}}}\n' $i $i; done > /tmp/p.ndjson; post /tmp/p.ndjson; printf '%s\n' '{"title":"direct","gid":1}' | curl -sS -X POST "http://localhost:9308/bulk?bulk_import=system.bb_s0&shared" -H 'Content-Type: application/x-ndjson' --data-binary @- -w ' HTTP %{http_code}\n'; sql "PURGE BULK_IMPORT FROM TABLE bb OPTION clear_sessions=1"; echo "children=$(ps -eo args | grep -c '[i]ndexer_rt_bulk_chunk')"; commit; counts
